  "title": "The sus4 chord",
  "summary": "Swap the 3rd for a 4th, and it wants to fall back.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Sus4",
      "body": "A **sus4** chord uses a perfect 4th in place of the 3rd. Csus4 is C F G. The 4th leans on the 3rd below it, so the chord wants to fall back to C major.\n\n**Why it matters:** Sus4 to major is one of the most common moves in songs, often right at the end of a phrase. When you hear the chord \"settle\", that is often a sus4 resolving.",
